summary:
  This daily radiology news briefing highlights practice-changing research in Alzheimer's detection, AI governance, and cardiovascular health. Key updates also include advancements in lung infection treatment and insights into the impact of weight-loss drugs on consumer spending.

top_stories[8]{title,source,url,category,importance,ai_summary}:
  Title: "Lessons on AI governance from the radiology department"
  Source: Healthcare IT News
  URL: https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMihwFBVV95cUxOemRkTmxZZmNmQ2RaUkFpNXprMTRxS0Qzc2g4RWJGVG02bmtyRGhJWnV0Ukd0dGRNeGZFS3J5Y1hzMnZValZiUC1zdUJ2aExybVBabURtWkNDa3Zza0pXSVZmU0hNQW9Pd0...test that tracks individual bacteria to see which drugs truly eliminate them. When tested on tuberculosis and other serious lung infections, the method revealed big differences in how bacteria tolerate treatment. The findings could lead to more precise therapies and better predictions of treatment success.
  Category: ir
  importance: 95
  ai_summary: "A new method tracks individual bacteria to understand drug effectiveness in lung infections, potentially leading to personalized therapies."
  
  Title: "A hidden brain signal may reveal Alzheimer’s long before diagnosis"
